<article class="env-lemma" id="02GG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02GG">Lemma <span data-tag="02GG">29.36.16</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of schemes over $S$. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
If $X$ is unramified over $S$, then $f$ is unramified. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $X$ is G-unramified over $S$ and $Y$ is locally of finite type over $S$, then $f$ is G-unramified. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assume that $X$ is unramified over $S$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/01T8" data-tag="01T8">29.15.8</a> we see that $f$ is locally of finite type. By assumption we have $\Omega _{X/S} = 0$. Hence $\Omega _{X/Y} = 0$ by Lemma <a href="/tag/01UX" data-tag="01UX">29.33.9</a>. Thus $f$ is unramified. If $X$ is G-unramified over $S$ and $Y$ is locally of finite type over $S$, then by Lemma <a href="/tag/02FV" data-tag="02FV">29.22.11</a> we see that $f$ is locally of finite presentation and we conclude that $f$ is G-unramified. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>